raml_name — this is not simply "description if present, else key." Apply this 3-way classification (in order):
No description at all (raml_description is None) → raml_name = "Not Present". Note reason: "Description is not mentioned in RAML file".
Description equals the key, case-insensitively (i.e. identical once both are lowercased — this covers exact matches and pure-casing differences like buildingName vs BuildingName) → raml_name = raml_key (use the key's own casing). No mismatch is flagged for this case, even though the raw strings differ in case.
Description looks like natural-language prose — heuristic: it contains a period, or a comma followed by a lowercase word, or 4+ whitespace-separated words, or common sentence glue-words ("and", "the", "is", "during", "originally", "applicable", etc.) → treat it as a real explanatory description, not a name. raml_name = raml_key. No mismatch flagged. (Example: cacheID's description "cacheID, applicable during requotes and mid term adjustments..." falls here — display just cacheID.)
