6. Overall Result and Notes/Comments — the actual pass/fail rule

Compute these five independent checks per row. Overall Result = FAIL if any one of them is true; otherwise PASS. This exact rule reproduced 273/275 rows of the reference report with zero deviation:

Path check: raml_path != map_path (this is what column G reports as Fail).
Name/description check: raml_name != map_name (plain string inequality, independent of the path check — a row can have matching paths but a mismatched name, and vice versa).
Type check: after normalizing both sides with the synonym table in §2/§3, norm(raml_type) != norm(map_type). Important: number and double are treated as genuinely different types and always fail this check — they are not synonyms, unlike the date/time/integer/boolean/string variants.
Type-missing check: one side has a type value and the other is blank.
Mandatory/Optional check: convert raml_required to text (True → "Mandatory", False → "Optional") and compare to map_mandatory verbatim. Mismatch → fail. (If map_mandatory is something other than exactly Mandatory or Optional, e.g. Not present, treat this check as inapplicable and rely on the path/name checks instead.)

Notes/Comments — build by concatenating, in this fixed order, only the checks that failed, joined with " and ":

Failed check	Phrase to use
Name check, raml_name == "Not Present" (no description)	Description is not mentioned in RAML file
Name check, description present but differs from key, no space in it	Tag name mismatch
Name check, description present but differs from key, contains a space	Field name mismatch
Type check (real mismatch, e.g. number/double) — standalone, no other check failed	Data Type mismatch (with a space, capital T)
Type check (real mismatch) — combined with any other failed check	Datatype mismatch (no space, lowercase t)
Type-missing check	Data type missing from mapping document (or ...from RAML file if it's the RAML side that's blank)
Mandatory/Optional check	Mandatory/Optional parameter mismatch
Row unmatched — no RAML path at all	Not present in mapping document (mapping side) / symmetric wording if the RAML side is the one missing

Concatenate multiple failed checks with " and ", in this fixed order: name → type → mandatory. (One row in the reference report reverses type-before-name; treat that as a one-off inconsistency, not a rule to replicate.)

